# Figma: faithful structure + split breakpoints

## Breakpoints

| Prefix | Width |
| --- | --- |
| base (no prefix) | < 440px |
| `tb:` | 440px |
| `dk:` | 1025px |
| `dk-lg:` | 1600px |

`get_design_context` is a **reference**. Extra `div`s for `rotate`, `flex-none`, `hypot()`, or `cqw` are codegen, not layers. Trust **`data-name`** and the Figma tree.

In `.astro`, the attribute is `class`, not `className`. `cn` is exported from `src/lib/cn.ts`. From a section file:

```astro
import { cn } from '../../../../lib/cn';
```

## 1. One Figma node → one DOM node

- 1 Auto Layout / frame → 1 element.
- 1 image node → 1 wrapper + `<img>`. Put `rounded-*`, `rotate-*`, `aspect-*`, and position **on that wrapper**.
- Do not add shells around rotation or absolute children unless that frame exists in Figma.

```astro
<!-- MCP soup -->
<div class="flex h-[23.5rem] items-center">
  <div class="-rotate-3 flex-none">
    <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-[1.25rem] aspect-[3/2]">
      <img />
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- matches “about imagery > img 2” -->
<div class="-rotate-3 overflow-hidden rounded-[1.25rem] aspect-[3/2] w-full">
  <img class="size-full object-cover" alt="" />
</div>
```

## 2. Figma components first, then the section

If the target frame (or its children) uses **component instances** (`<instance …>` in `get_metadata`, or repeated identical subtrees with the same `data-name`):

1. **Find** every distinct component used (by instance name / main-component link) — e.g. `seal`, `card`, `stat`, `button`.
2. **Build each as its own `.astro` file first** — open the **main component** (or one representative instance) with `get_design_context` + `get_variable_defs` at base, tb, dk, and dk-lg as needed.
3. Map Figma **component properties / variants / text overrides** to Astro props (`interface Props` + `Astro.props`): content, image, tone, **size**, and so on.
4. **Only then** build the section layout and **compose** those components.

### Component properties & variants

Figma **component sets** expose properties (`size`, `state`, `tone`, boolean toggles, text/image slots). The Astro component must mirror them — do not collapse variants into `tb:` / `dk:` / `dk-lg:` unless the Figma file itself is a single variant that only changes by breakpoint.

1. Open the **main component** (or each variant node) in Dev Mode / `get_design_context`.
2. List every **component property** and its allowed values (e.g. `size`: `small` | `medium` | `large`).
3. Implement **one Astro prop per property**, same names when sensible (`size`, not `property1`).
4. Build a **styles map** keyed by variant value — pull numbers from `get_variable_defs` **on that variant node**, not from MCP fallbacks.
5. The **section** picks the variant per breakpoint tree and passes it down:

```astro
---
// Seal.astro — one prop per Figma property
interface Props {
  size: 'small' | 'medium' | 'large';
}
const { size } = Astro.props;
---
```

```astro
<!-- section file: do not fold the variant into responsive utilities -->
<Seal class="tb:w-[14.4375rem] dk:w-[16.625rem]" />

<!-- section file: pass the Figma `size` prop; each tree picks its variant -->
<Seal size="large" />
<Seal size="medium" />
<Seal size="small" />
```

Do not substitute a Figma variant (`size=small`) with breakpoint CSS on a single component unless Figma has no variant and only tokens change at `tb` / `dk` / `dk-lg`.

**Image frames inside a component:** use the **visible crop / mask / frame** dimensions from the design for `aspect-*` or `w` / `h` — see `alc-advanced-layouts-to-code` (never the raw asset’s intrinsic ratio). One wrapper, as in section 1.

Do not inline-copy the same seal or card markup four times inside the section. Do not start the section file until the piece exists and matches Figma.

```astro
---
import Seal from './Seal.astro';
const seals = [];
---

<!-- component first — Figma `size` variant as a prop -->
<section>
  {seals.map((item) => <Seal size="large" {...item} />)}
</section>
```

Reuse an existing project component only if it already matches that Figma component; otherwise create one named after the Figma component (`Seal`, not `SealsSectionCard`).

Nested instances (a card that contains a badge): **innermost first**, then parents, then the section.

### Where to put the file

Page sections live under the page, as `.astro`. Section-local pieces are **siblings** of the section file — one file, no nested `components/` folder, no barrel.

```
src/pages/<Page>/_components/<SectionName>/
  index.astro
  Seal.astro
```

| Scope | Path |
| --- | --- |
| **Default** — built for one section only | `src/pages/<Page>/_components/<SectionName>/<ComponentName>.astro` |
| **Explicitly shared** — user says reuse / design system | `src/components/<ComponentName>/index.astro` |

Import the section-local piece with `import Seal from './Seal.astro';`.

```
src/components/Seal/index.astro

src/pages/Home/_components/SealsSection/components/Seal/index.astro

src/pages/Home/_components/SealsSection/
  index.astro
  Seal.astro
```

The first path puts a section-only piece in `src/components/`. The second adds a folder and a barrel inside the section. The third is the default: `index.astro` is the section, `Seal.astro` is the sibling.

Promote to `src/components/<ComponentName>/index.astro` only when the user asks, or when a second section needs the same component.

## 3. Desktop first, then smaller frames — two trees if layout differs

Resolve **base (< 440px), tb (440px), dk (1025px), and dk-lg (1600px)** on each frame.

If Figma frames are **not** the same tree (different parent, absolute vs flow, order, overlap):

1. Build the larger tree so it matches that node (often `dk` / `dk-lg`).
2. Build the compact tree so it matches the smaller nodes (base and `tb` may share one tree).
3. Toggle with `hidden` / `dk:hidden`. Do not morph one DOM with a pile of `tb:` / `dk:` / `dk-lg:` on every inset.

```astro
<div class="hidden dk:block">{/* dk + dk-lg layout — inside the max-w container */}</div>
<div class="dk:hidden">{/* base + tb layout */}</div>
```

Same tree at all sizes (only padding, type, or gap change) → **one** DOM + `tb:` / `dk:` / `dk-lg:` is fine. Omit a later prefix when the value matches the previous tier.

Apply the same split **inside** a component when its internal layout differs by breakpoint.

Layout variants are **`<div>` siblings** inside one section shell — not a second `<section>` per breakpoint.

### Section shell (one `<section>` per Figma section frame)

The section file owns the shell. Padding and max width belong to the Figma **section frame**, not to each layout variant.

```astro
---
import { cn } from '../../../../lib/cn';
import CommunityInfoSectionDesktop from './CommunityInfoSectionDesktop.astro';
import CommunityInfoSectionCompact from './CommunityInfoSectionCompact.astro';
---

<!-- one <section> — padding + max-w; variants are layout-only divs -->
<section
  class={cn(
    'relative w-full',
    'px-4 tb:px-10 dk:px-20',
    'pt-[1.75rem] tb:pt-10 dk:pt-[7.5rem]',
    'pb-[3.25rem] tb:pb-20 dk:pb-[7.5rem]',
  )}
>
  <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[100rem]">
    <CommunityInfoSectionDesktop />
    <CommunityInfoSectionCompact />
  </div>
</section>
```

| Layer | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `<section>` | Full width; **section padding** with `tb:` / `dk:` / `dk-lg:` from `get_variable_defs` on the section frame |
| Inner `div` | `mx-auto w-full max-w-[100rem]` — caps content at the dk-lg frame (1600px) |
| Layout variants | `hidden` / `dk:hidden` toggles + internal `gap`, order, stagger only. No padding on these |

`CommunityInfoSectionDesktop` is `hidden dk:flex`. `CommunityInfoSectionCompact` is `dk:hidden`.

Full-bleed backgrounds stay on `<section>` (`absolute`, edge-to-edge). Padding and `max-w` sit inside, or on the section with content in the centered column — never clip a bleed with `max-w` on the outermost node.

Resolve **section-frame** padding once on the section; do not repeat it on the layout children.

## 4. Sizes: resolve per breakpoint

Token **names** in `get_design_context` often look the same (`spacing-8xl`, `Display lg`, `radius-xl`) but the **resolved px change by breakpoint**. The codegen fallback (e.g. `spacing-2xl,32px`) is frequently wrong.

### Mandatory checks

For **base, tb, dk, and dk-lg** nodes separately, call Figma MCP **`get_variable_defs`** on:

- the section / Auto Layout frame (padding, gap)
- **each Figma component** you implement (not only the outer section)
- text layers (font size)
- cards / media frames (radius, border)

Record the **resolved number**, then convert to rem. Not the fallback in the class string.

| Concern | Examples to verify |
| --- | --- |
| Spacing | `spacing-*` → `px` / `py` / `pt` / `pb` / `gap` |
| Typography | `Body/*`, `Heading/*`, `Display/*`, or project classes like `h1` / `body-1` → `text-[…]` in rem |
| Radius | `radius-*` → `rounded-[…]` |
| Other sizes | fixed `w` / `h` / offsets from layout (still rem) |

### Never

```astro
<!-- trusting MCP fallback — base spacing-2xl was 16, not 32 -->
class="px-[var(--spacing-2xl,32px)]"

<!-- one size for all breakpoints when variables differ -->
class="text-[4.875rem]"
```

### Do

```astro
<!-- after get_variable_defs on each breakpoint node -->
<!-- base 16, tb 40, dk 80 — omit dk-lg when it matches dk -->
class="px-4 tb:px-10 dk:px-20"

<!-- base 40, tb 60, dk 78. Append dk-lg:text-[…] only when 1600px resolves to a different px. -->
class="text-[2.5rem] tb:text-[3.75rem] dk:text-[4.875rem]"

<!-- base 14, tb 18, dk 20 -->
class="rounded-[0.875rem] tb:rounded-[1.125rem] dk:rounded-[1.25rem]"
```

If the project already has CSS tokens that switch at `tb` / `dk` / `dk-lg`, map to those instead of hardcoding rem — still read each breakpoint once.

## 5. Units: rem

When project CSS tokens are missing:

- Convert resolved Figma **px → rem** with root **16**: `value / 16`.
- Arbitrary Tailwind: `py-[3.25rem]`, `text-[1.375rem]`, `rounded-[0.875rem]`.
- Prefer scale utilities (`gap-6`, `px-4`, `px-10`) **only when they equal** the resolved rem.
- Keep **%** for Scale constraints; unitless or `%` line-heights; **deg** for rotate.
- Do not ship `…px` in `class`.

## 6. Order of work

1. base / tb / dk / dk-lg nodes (`get_metadata` / `get_design_context`) — note any `<instance>` / shared components.
2. **Implement each Figma component** (properties → Astro props → styles map → rem via `get_variable_defs` per variant) **before** the section. Default path: `src/pages/<Page>/_components/<SectionName>/<ComponentName>.astro`.
3. **One section shell** (`<section>` + padding + `max-w-[100rem]`) + layout variants as `<div>` children.
4. Apply **resolved** rem (or project tokens) with `tb:` / `dk:` / `dk-lg:` on the shell and on layout internals as needed.
5. Order classes (`ots-order-tailwindcss-styles`) and commit raw images (`di-download-raw-images`).
